      "values": []
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "34e5aa3b-db10-40a1-893d-79e98cd3f2f4",
      "key": "597bab26-b2a5-448b-801f-48d590823c13",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Features"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHalf board accommodation\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll excursions \u0026amp; guided tours included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlue Badge guide in Isle of Wight\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EReturn Wightlink ferry crossing from Portsmouth\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExecutive coach throughout\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EONE FREE PLACE PER 10 PAYING PASSENGERS\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1d09b5af-b95a-4af5-b8f2-323db029e817",
      "key": "81fb8d8c-34dc-4531-b677-a67f19ca6465",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Accommodation"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFour nights on half board basis at the centrally located 3* The Royal Esplanade Hotel at Ryde. Facilities at the hotel include a restaurant and bar. All rooms are en suite.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2d9b0603-29ef-423a-8d3e-d9c039d3d7b1",
      "key": "2432fb5f-e151-4804-9500-145f40492150",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMottisfont Abbey Garden, House \u0026amp; Estate, Hants\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECircular tour of the island\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Needles, Alum Bay \u0026amp; Cowes\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOsborne House\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHistoric village of Godshill\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESteam railway trip\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERyde\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHistoric town of Newport\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECarisbrooke Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESandown\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EKingston Lacy, Wimborne\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "de535189-b468-4594-8118-f303bac50e3c",
      "key": "9ea03b6f-9403-440c-96f7-edf5ec4298b8",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tailor your sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFarringford - a Grade I listed building, the home of Alfred Lord Tennyson attracted many of the Poet Laureate\u2019s eminent friends, becoming a locus of intellectual and artistic activity\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll Saints\u2019 Church at Godshill - mentioned in the Doomsday Book, All Saints is renowned for its mid-15th century mural of the Lily Cross\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAppuldurcombe House - the shell of a fine 18th century Baroque style house, once the grandest house on the island, stands in \u2018Capability\u2019 Brown grounds and an exhibition of photographs and prints depicts the house and its history\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Here are some more suggested places of interest you might like to include:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "20ff1f8d-30c2-4693-8f84-e7bbba04c932",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1 \u2013 Mottisfont Abbey Garden, House \u0026amp; Estate\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBoard our private executive coach at your preferred pick up points \u2013 visit en route a suitable National Trust property such as Mottisfont Abbey Garden, House and Estate in Romsey, a 12th century Augustine priory that is now a handsome house whose grounds offer a magnificent collection of trees, walled gardens and a National Collection of old fashioned roses \u2013 Wightlink ferry crossing from Portsmouth to Fishbourne \u2013 check in to the 3* The Royal Esplanade Hotel at Ryde.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2 \u2013 Island tour \u0026amp; Osborne House\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ECircular tour of the island with our Blue Badge guide taking in The Needles, Alum Bay and the historic port of Cowes \u2013 Osborne House was demolished after Queen Victoria and Prince Albert bought Osborne and its estate in 1845 and a new three storey pavilion was built.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3 \u2013 Godshill, steam railway trip \u0026amp; Ryde\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ETime at leisure in Godshill to explore the historic village, to visit the 14th century church that sits on a small hillock overlooking the village or to explore the model village \u2013 at Havenstreet we take a ride on the Isle of Wight\u0026#39;s restored steam railway in Victorian and Edwardian carriages dating back to 1876, a unique way to experience the atmosphere of bygone train travel \u2013 finish the day at the resort of Ryde with its sweeping sandy bay and delightful pier.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4 \u2013 Newport, Carisbrooke Castle \u0026amp; Sandown\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EVisit the beautiful and historic town of Newport \u2013 Carisbrooke Castle is the island\u2019s royal fortress and prison to King Charles I before his execution in London in 1648 \u2013 time at leisure to explore the resort of Sandown with its beautiful sandy beach that slopes gently into the sea.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5 \u2013 Kingston Lacy\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWightlink ferry crossing from Fishbourne to Portsmouth \u2013 en route home visit a suitable National Trust property such as Kingston Lacy Mansion in Wimborne, dating from 17th century with beautiful interiors and garden and one of the greatest family picture collections in the UK.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Suggested Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Every one of our tours is exclusively for your group and your group alone so each one can be tailor made to suit the interests and profile of your members until you have a tour with an itinerary and at a price which matches the interests and profile of your members."
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "Remember this itinerary is just our suggestion. "
          }
        }
      ]
    },
